## D-280 (decisions.md l.7)
7:| D-280 | 2026-11-16 | delivery-orchestrator | **DG7 round 6 outcome on 0b481627, the disclosure repair, and round 7.** Domain, code-security and qa all PASS on the same candidate; all three verified F-DG7-971 closed. They raised one shared Low gap under three ids (F-DG7-923, 942, 972): ADR-0064 A5.6 requires the D-278 drill disclosure in `known-limitations.md`, the release notes and the Arabic summaries, and only `deployment.md` carried it. Low findings do not block a gate, but A5.6 is mandatory text of an accepted ADR, so it is repaired before the audit rather than waived. AN-P7I wrote the disclosure text (it could not write `docs/handover/**`, its write scope); DO-D10 applied it verbatim to `known-limitations.md`, `deployment.md`, both Arabic summaries and the handover README, and added a release-notes section read from the checked-in `tools/release/release-notes-disclosures.json`, with tests (14/14) and a mutation check. **ADR-0071 §5.1 note:** the release-notes generator now reads that one extra checked-in file of its own, in the way `claims-scan.mjs` reads its allow-list; I accept this as within ADR-0071's intent (deterministic output from checked-in inputs) and record it here instead of amending the ADR. The secret-scan history scope then flagged two lines of the round-6 QA records that quote the reviewer's own secret-search grep pattern; they are regexes, not credentials, and are allow-listed by value hash for the history scope only (as earlier delivery-record entries are). Pre-freeze r7: 17/19 exit 0 at first run; secret-payload and release-tool-tests failed because the two new entries were stale in the payload scope; after scoping them to history, those checks were re-run (prefreeze-r7b). Arabic text stays provisional (`arabic-review.json` is empty). Engine ticks (A5.7 residual 3) stay undecided and disclosed as not covered. | Round-6 records under `docs/delivery/reviews/DG7/round-6/`; handbacks T-DG7-AN-P7I and T-DG7-DO-D10; `test-evidence/DG7/orchestrator/prefreeze-r7` and `prefreeze-r7b`. | A reviewer finds the disclosure inaccurate or a surface still missing; ADR-0071's owner rejects the extra input file. |
